# Makefile lines that may still run a BARE uv -- read by
# scripts/check_uv_pin.py, rule 4 (doppler#2369). A RATCHET: it only shrinks.
#
# Every other uv call in a makefile is spelled $(UV), so `UV=<the pinned uv>`
# -- the way out on a box whose uv is not the pin -- reaches it. Each line
# here is `<text found in the makefile line> -- <why it stays bare>`; a line
# with no reason is refused, and an entry whose text no longer appears in any
# makefile fails the gate, so it is deleted in the change that retires its
# reason. Text, not a line number, so unrelated edits do not move it.

PYTHON_EXECUTABLE ?= $(shell uv run python -c -- #2364: PR #2368 rewrites this probe (it needs $(or $(UV),uv), since UV is defined later in the file); drop this line when it lands
uv run python scripts/list_hand_ext_c.py; } -- #2361: PR #2365 rewrites C_FILES through $(UV); drop this line when it lands
